     "email": "fgghklkkjg@outlook.com",
     "date": "2026-09-04T11:35:25Z"
    },
    "message": "ci(desktop): let a shell-release dispatch build a different ref than it uploads to\n\nThe first dispatch against v6.43.0 failed on all four legs in under a minute:\n\"The directory name is invalid ... /desktop-shell/src-tauri\". The workflow\nchecked out the tag it was uploading to, and v6.43.0 predates #272, so there\nwas no shell in that tree to build.\n\nOn `release: published` building the tag is right and must stay: the tag\ncarries the source the release is made of. A dispatch is the case where the two\nquestions differ -- backfilling assets onto a release published before the\nshell existed, or before a fix to this workflow landed, means uploading *to*\nthat tag while building something newer. So `tag` now means where the assets\ngo, and a new optional `ref` means what to build, defaulting to `tag`.\n\nA guard step reports a checkout with no desktop-shell/ in it once, naming the\nref and the fix, instead of letting four legs fail on a working directory that\ndoes not exist.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01JsSZ8AQXV1XKgKkgYBU5UT",
